{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you.</b> The forsaken ones — a descriptive noun on the pattern of יראים (1 Samuel 23:3)." "<b>For Gad.</b> A constellation of the heavens. Rabbi Moses the Kohen says that Gad is the planet Jupiter, which indicates everything good, for so is the language of Kedar. And he said that there is none like it in בא גד (Genesis 30:11)." "<b>For Meni.</b> Some say: for a figure of the sphere, for each and every figure has a known number of stars. And Rabbi Moses the Kohen said that it is the name of a star." "<b>From the bowl.</b> From the root of מסכה יינה (Proverbs 9:2)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:02.763459740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}